// Title: Suspicious Process Start Locations
// Sigma ID: 15b75071-74cc-47e0-b4c6-b43744a62a2b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: juju4, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-01-16 | Modified: 2022-01-07
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036
// Tags: car.2013-05-002
// Description: Detects suspicious process run from unusual locations
// False positives:
//   - False positives depend on scripts and administrative tools used in the monitored environment
// References:
//   - https://car.mitre.org/wiki/CAR-2013-05-002
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_run_locations.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains ":\\RECYCLER\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\SystemVolumeInformation\\") or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\Tasks\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\debug\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\fonts\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\help\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\drivers\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\addins\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\cursors\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\system32\\tasks\\")
